BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rijkscultuurfondsen-interdisciplinary-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T075436Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Rijkscultuurfondsen: Interdisciplinary Grant
DESCRIPTION:The Interdisciplinary grant is a new joint scheme of the six Du
 tch national cultural funds (Mondriaan Fund\, Performing Arts Fund NL\, Fu
 nd for Cultural Participation\, Netherlands Film Fund\, Creative Industrie
 s Fund NL\, and the Dutch Foundation for Literature)\, announced on 7 July
  2026. It supports makers and organisations whose work genuinely crosses t
 he boundaries of the individual funds' disciplines (visual art\, design\, 
 film\, literature\, performing arts\, and cultural participation) and cann
 ot be contained within a single discipline. TWO TRACKS: an Individual trac
 k for professional makers with a demonstrable interdisciplinary practice (
 at least one year of experience\; income cap EUR 55\,000 including the gra
 nt\; approximately EUR 24\,900 for 12 months)\; and an Organisation track 
 for non-profit cultural organisations with legal personality running multi
 -discipline projects that genuinely integrate disciplines rather than pres
 enting them side by side\, in two fixed tiers: EUR 12\,500 for projects bu
 dgeted EUR 15\,000 to 60\,000\, or EUR 50\,000 for projects budgeted EUR 6
 0\,000 to 500\,000. The individual contribution can only be awarded once p
 er maker\, and students in a bachelor's\, master's or PhD programme cannot
  apply. ELIGIBILITY: makers and organisations based in the Netherlands or 
 the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. APPLYING: handled through the Mondriaan
  Fund's online application portal (info@mondriaanfonds.nl)\; an account is
  required in advance. DEADLINE: 1 October 2026\, 16:00 Dutch time (11:00 C
 aribbean time\; single application round).\n\nOrganisation: Dutch national
  cultural funds (Rijkscultuurfondsen)\, via the Mondriaan Fund\nLocation: 
 Netherlands. For professional makers and organisations based in the Nether
 lands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans multiple d
 isciplines.\nAward: Individual-maker track: EUR 24\,900 for 12 months (inc
 ome cap EUR 55\,000 including the grant\; awarded once per maker). Organis
 ation track\, two fixed tiers: EUR 12\,500 for projects budgeted EUR 15\,0
 00 to 60\,000\, or EUR 50\,000 for projects budgeted EUR 60\,000 to 500\,0
 00. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to 12 months for the individual-make
 r track.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grant
 s/interdisciplinary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refe
 rral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/interdiscipli
 nary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. For professional makers and organisations based in th
 e Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans mu
 ltiple disciplines.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-design-sector-internationalisation-2026@artificialnou
 veau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T075436Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260923
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Design Sector Internationalisation Gra
 nt Scheme 2026
DESCRIPTION:This scheme funds international activity by the Dutch design\, 
 architecture and digital culture sectors\, covering projects that take pla
 ce mainly abroad and require at least one international partner. Open to p
 rofessional makers\, observers\, design agencies and cultural institutions
 . Grants run EUR 10\,000 to EUR 50\,000 with at least 20 percent co-financ
 ing. The round runs 25 August 2026\, 15:00 CEST to 22 September 2026\, 16:
 00 CEST. From 2026 places are allocated by lottery draw rather than order 
 of submission. Activities in countries under a code-red travel advisory or
  subject to sanctions are excluded. Applicants must be registered with the
  Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK).\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creat
 ieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocation: Netherlands-based 
 applicants\; funded activity takes place mainly abroad. At least one inter
 national partner required.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 to EUR 50\,000. Minimum 20 
 percent co-financing. Round budget EUR 300\,000 (2026 total EUR 600\,000).
  No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; activities take place main
 ly abroad.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/design-sect
 or-internationalisation-grant-scheme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/design-sector-internationali
 sation-grant-scheme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based applicants\; funded activity takes place mainly 
 abroad. At least one international partner required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T075436Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-art-projects-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T075436Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Art Projects
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Art Projects scheme contributes to the co
 sts of realising a contemporary art project. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, cura
 tors\, critics\, publicists\, partnerships and organisations. Applicants d
 o not have to live in The Hague: Hague artists apply via their Stroom data
 base registration (Mijn Stroom)\, while applicants from outside the city a
 pply with a CV\, provided the project takes place in The Hague or otherwis
 e benefits art and artists in The Hague. ASSESSMENT: quality and distincti
 veness of the project\, whether it represents a step in a new direction\, 
 an experiment or a departure\, its contribution to The Hague's art climate
 \, and proportionality between budget and scope. APPLICATION: via the Stro
 om portal with a plan of max 2\,500 words (artistic rationale\, target aud
 ience\, evaluation)\, an itemised budget using Stroom's model\, and image 
 documentation. NOT ELIGIBLE: applications connected to formal (art) educat
 ion programmes or from current students (Bachelor\, Master\, postdoc\, PhD
 ). DEADLINE: the last 2026 round closes 25 October 2026 (rounds recur roug
 hly every six weeks through the year). The grant is valid for up to two ye
 ars after the decision\, with 80 percent paid upfront.\n\nOrganisation: St
 room Den Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicants from 
 outside The Hague (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes place in 
 The Hague or otherwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hague artis
 ts must be registered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).\nAward: Maximu
 m EUR 10\,000 per project\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant per calendar y
 ear. Requests above EUR 5\,000 require at least 30 percent co-financing of
  the total budget from third parties. Artist fees\, production and communi
 cation costs are eligible\; Stroom endorses the kunstenaarshonorarium.nl f
 ee guideline. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the grant rem
 ains valid for up to two years after the decision meeting\, with 80 percen
 t paid upfront and 20 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https://www.str
 oom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-projects?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-p
 rojects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicants from outside The Hague
  (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes place in The Hague or othe
 rwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hague artists must be regist
 ered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-seed-grant-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T075436Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Seed Grant\, Autumn 2026 round
DESCRIPTION:The Stokroos Seed Grant supports early-practice visual artists\
 , designers and craft practitioners in the Netherlands with an unrestricte
 d budget for a self-defined plan: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\, EUR 7\,500 
 for duos\, EUR 10\,000 for collectives. The plan must start at least 10 we
 eks after submission\, last no longer than a year\, and can take place any
 where in the world. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: makers who between 2018 and 2022 comp
 leted their first subject-specific HBO or MBO programme\, or started their
  practice without formal training (first public presentation or commission
  marks the start)\; at least 21 years old\; living and working in the King
 dom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at 
 least one year\; not enrolled in a study or post-academic programme during
  the grant period. RESTRICTIONS: one application per person every two cale
 ndar years\, a lifetime maximum of two Seed Grants\, and only one applicat
 ion per year across all Stokroos schemes. DEADLINE: the autumn window runs
  1 September to 31 October 2026\, but the form CLOSES EARLY once 60 eligib
 le applications are received\, so apply as soon as possible. TO APPLY: onl
 ine form (Dutch or English) with portfolio PDF (max 20 pages\, 10MB)\, CV\
 , work and plan descriptions and a timeline\; response within about 8 week
 s. Recipients acknowledge Stokroos in communication about the plan.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLocation: Applicants must live and work in 
 the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean parts) or Suriname
  for at least one year\; the funded plan itself can take place anywhere in
  the world.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\, EUR 7\,500 for duos\, EUR
  10\,000 for collectives\, as an unrestricted contribution to a self-defin
 ed plan. No application fee.\nDuration: Funded plan starts at least 10 wee
 ks after submission and lasts up to one year\n\nMore: https://stokroos.nl/
 en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (i
 ncluding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; the fund
 ed plan itself can take place anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cifnl-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T075436Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Industries Fund NL: Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL offers one residency at Videota
 ge\, the Hong Kong media art institute (est. 1986) known for critical work
  on XR\, AI\, blockchain and video games. The 2027 edition takes the techn
 ological 'black box' phenomenon as its starting point: deep neural network
 s now shape social media\, healthcare\, finance\, governance and justice w
 hile their inner workings remain hard to grasp\, and the resident is invit
 ed to explore this through media art in Hong Kong's urban context. WHO: an
  individual designer\, maker or observer within digital culture\, establis
 hed in the Netherlands or the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom\, registered 
 with the KvK (or another Kingdom business register)\, with at least four y
 ears of professional practice. NOT for duos\, collectives\, or recipients 
 of CIFNL Talent Development\, Self-taught Designer or Emerging Design Prac
 tices ABCSSS grants during the work period (winning this excludes applying
  to those schemes in 2027). SUPPORT: EUR 5\,000 (two months) or EUR 6\,500
  (three months) for travel\, insurance\, living costs\, time and materials
 \; housing\, workspace\, curatorial guidance and production costs are paid
  directly to Videotage\; accommodation arranged by Videotage\; access to e
 quipment and the Videotage Media Art Collection archive. SELECTION: tender
 -style ranking by an external advisory committee on artistic quality\, pro
 ject quality and motivation\; the top five proposals go to Videotage\, whi
 ch co-decides\; decision within eight weeks of closing. APPLY via the Fund
 's application platform (aanvragen.stimuleringsfonds.nl)\, round 'Open Cal
 l Residencies 2027'\, preferably in English: work plan (max 4 A4 / 4 MB PD
 F)\, brief CV (max 2 A4)\, portfolio (max 8 A4 / 8 MB)\, certified KvK ext
 ract under one year old\, and a representative JPG image. NOTE: account ac
 tivation on the platform takes one working day\, so register early. DEADLI
 NE: 21 October 2026\, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Industries Fun
 d NL (Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie)\, with Videotage\nLocation: H
 ong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in the Neth
 erlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarte
 n and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business register (KvK)
 .\nAward: One residency grant: EUR 5\,000 for a two-month work period or E
 UR 6\,500 for three months\, covering travel\, insurance\, living expenses
 \, compensation for time invested\, and material and transport costs. Hous
 ing\, work space\, Videotage guidance and production costs are paid by the
  Fund directly to Videotage on top of the grant\; accommodation is arrange
 d by Videotage. No application fee.\nDuration: 23 March to 18 May 2027 (tw
 o months) or 23 March to 15 June 2027 (three months)\; state your preferre
 d period. Research period plus a concluding public presentation event for 
 Videotage's Hong Kong network.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/e
 n/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in
  the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Si
 nt Maarten and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business regis
 ter (KvK).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nl-embassy-brussels-cultural-support-nov-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261030T075436Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherlands Embassy in Brussels: Open Call for Cultural P
 roject Support
DESCRIPTION:The Netherlands Embassy in Brussels runs several open calls per
  year subsidising Dutch-Belgian artistic and cultural projects in Belgium 
 that strengthen the Netherlands' cultural profile and promote cooperation 
 between the two countries. All artistic disciplines are eligible\, with a 
 focus on performing arts\, visual arts\, cultural heritage\, creative indu
 stries and digital culture\; the embassy welcomes innovative formats\, cro
 ss-border exchange\, and work on participation\, inclusion\, equal rights 
 and sustainability. The subsidy (max EUR 5\,000) only covers costs related
  to the Dutch participation in the project\, such as travel and accommodat
 ion for Dutch participants\, art transport\, production\, and communicatio
 n for the Dutch segment. Projects must take place in Belgium (unless virtu
 al collaborations) and be accessible to the public\; personal development 
 projects are not eligible. ELIGIBILITY: professional creators\, organisati
 ons\, institutions and legal entities in Belgium with a company registrati
 on number\; Dutch artists typically take part via a Belgian partner or org
 aniser. Apply via the embassy (netherlandsandyou.nl). DEADLINES: 3 Novembe
 r 2026\, then 18 March 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Embassy of the Kingdom of th
 e Netherlands in Brussels\nLocation: Belgium. Applicants must be professio
 nal creators\, organisations\, institutions or legal entities in Belgium w
 ith a company registration number\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of D
 utch-Belgian projects.\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 per project.\nDuration: Ro
 lling open calls with multiple deadlines per year\; next deadlines 3 Novem
 ber 2026 and 18 March 2027.\n\nMore: https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlem
 bassy-brussels-open-call-for-support?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlembassy-brussels-open-call-for-suppo
 rt?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Belgium. Applicants must be professional creators\, organisations\
 , institutions or legal entities in Belgium with a company registration nu
 mber\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of Dutch-Belgian projects.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amsterdam-light-festival-open-call-edition-16@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261030T075436Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261208
SUMMARY:Deadline: Amsterdam Light Festival Edition 16 Open Call (light art\
 , EUR 4\,000 artist fee plus production costs)
DESCRIPTION:Amsterdam Light Festival invites light art concepts for its 16t
 h edition (2027-2028)\, presented along and on the canals of Amsterdam. WH
 O: creatives from all over the world\, individually or as a team\; multipl
 e submissions are allowed and existing work may be considered. A second st
 rand\, Open Call X Amarte (supported by the Amarte Fonds)\, is for makers 
 based in the Netherlands who are new to the medium of light art and seeks 
 concepts for walking visitors. WHAT YOU GET: an artist fee of EUR 4\,000\,
  with the costs of producing the artwork and travel covered\, plus technic
 al support from the festival\; Amarte selections receive an EUR 4\,000 fee
  and a EUR 20\,000 production budget. APPLICATION: read the Artist Briefin
 g\, fill in the submission template and submit via the portal linked from 
 the briefing\; see the FAQ at amsterdamlightfestival.com/en/faq-open-call.
  DEADLINE: 7 December 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Amsterdam Light F
 estival\nLocation: Amsterdam\, the Netherlands. Main call open to creative
 s worldwide\; the Open Call X Amarte strand is for Netherlands-based maker
